WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.490
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Welcome
to Deconstructing Chatbots.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.900
I am Priyanka Vergadia,
and in this episode,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.980
we will integrate Dialogflow
with Twilio's messaging

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.550
service.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.917
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.800
One of my friends uses
Twilio messaging service

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.200
and requested that I walk
him through setting up

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.870
Twilio bots with natural
language understanding

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.550
based on Dialogflow.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.100
So here we go.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.530
Again, we are going to work with
the same appointment scheduler

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.100
chatbot and integrate it with
Twilio's messaging service

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.860
so that our users
who choose to text us

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.580
can get the same experience
as the ones who are using us

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.400
on web and Google Home.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.930
We are in our agent.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.060
Let's click Integration.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.270
This time we are going to click
on Twilio's text messaging

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.010
service.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.800
The pop-up has some
instructions-- click on Start,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.620
copy the request URL, and
put it in the Twilio's

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.380
programmable SMS.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.760
There are more instructions;
if you click on the link,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.819
it takes you to the
detailed screenshots

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:06.350
and how to set it up.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.410
But for now, let's
just do it ourselves.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.600
The first thing you will
need is a Twilio account.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.950
If you don't have one,
create it and then log in.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.070
From the dashboard,
click on All the Products

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.670
and navigate to
Programmable SMS.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.860
Once you are on the Programmable
SMS dashboard, click on SMS.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.500
I already have an appointment
scheduled a messaging service

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.050
set up here, but you can
just create one for yourself,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.640
provide it a name,
and in the use case,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.370
select Chatbot
Interactive 2-Way.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.140
Let's click on the
messaging service you

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.690
created to assign
a phone number.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.510
Use the Add button to
buy a new phone number

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:50.300
or just use an existing
number if you have one.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.700
Click through the US
selections and you

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.920
should have a number assigned.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.290
Now we click on
the configuration

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.930
to integrate Dialogflow.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.510
Enable inbound settings.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.790
In the request
URL, copy and paste

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.630
the URL that was generated by
Dialogflow in the Integration

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:12.010
section and save it.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:16.270
Now copy the service ID, phone
number, and the auth token

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:19.990
from Twilio dashboard and
paste them in the Dialogflow

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.510
Integration Console again.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:27.420
Once you're done, click
on Save and start.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:27.930
Yay!

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.610
Our bot started successfully.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.300
Now it's time to test your
bot via text messages.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.050
So we will use the
number we assigned

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:41.430
to our messaging service and
run through that example again.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.480
Hi.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.370
I would like to set an
appointment for 3:00

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.030
PM tomorrow.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.220
Driver's license.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.550
Great, we received
a confirmation.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:58.050
All right.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.460
So today we integrated our
appointment scheduler chatbot

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.460
with Twilio messaging
service, enabling our users

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.680
to set an appointment via text.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.440
We managed to provide
the exact same experience

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.280
to our users using our bot
from the website or via text.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.690
Well, that's a win.

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:15.930
That's it for today.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.740
Join me in the next episode
for deconstructing chatbots

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.590
where we will learn
more about fulfillments.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.820
If you like this video
and want to see more,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.040
subscribe to our channel.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

